{"name":"Flowers of May","hex":"#e3d7e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flowers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of flower"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of flower"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flowers"},{"term":"may","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Malay."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be strong; to have power (over). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To be able; can."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/may"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"},{"title":"May","blocks":[{"text":"May is the fifth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Podophyllum_peltatum_Shenks_Ferry_2.jpg/330px-Podophyllum_peltatum_Shenks_Ferry_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/May"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Phalaenopsis_bellina_%28Blue_Pink_x_sib%29_%28Rchb.f.%29_Christenson-_Brittonia_